{"type":"text","timestamp":1794305407240,"sessionID":"ses_e3b1a1f1cffeoKy75KKm9mz8Jf","part":{"id":"prt_1c4ef6950001wxsxSTXbwJMK5b","sessionID":"ses_e3b1a1f1cffeoKy75KKm9mz8Jf","messageID":"msg_1c4ef5dc8001OMkAGxfHnRv6xK","type":"text","text":"All 3 tests pass. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n| File | Bug | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `money.py` | `int(float(amount) * 100)` — floating-point precision error (`\"19.99\"` → `1998`) | Use `Decimal(amount) * 100` for exact conversion |\n| `tax.py` | `net_cents * rate // 100` — integer truncation instead of rounding half-up (`399.8` → `399`) | Use `Decimal` with `ROUND_HALF_UP` to round `399.8` → `400` |\n| `invoice.py` | Discount was applied globally in `total()`, not per-line before tax | Each line's discount is computed with half-up rounding, subtracted to get the discounted net, and that net is used for both `net_cents()` and `tax_cents()` |","time":{"start":1794305386832,"end":1794305407240}}}
